      "role": "user",
      "content": "the risk assessment form is a good idea. i'm just worried about the actual execution on the night of the event. kitchens get so hectic during a busy service and things can get chaotic or overlooked easily. is there any way to frame the level of importance to the staff so they don't treat these requests as just another minor task? i want them to feel like these precautions are non-negotiable and part of the core service.",
      "source": "evaluator"
