    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is essential to emphasize the gravity of the situation and the non-negotiable nature of the dietary requirements. With the catering staff, hold a briefing meeting well before the event where you can create an understanding of the risks associated with allergic reactions, the domino effect on the firm's reputation and the potential legal implications. This meeting should also serve as a rehearsal for the night, so staff can practice and feel confident handling these serious requests amidst their busy service. You can also provide mandatory training or a quick refresher on dealing with allergies and dietary restrictions, ensuring everyone understands and adheres to these non-negotiable standards.\n\nAdditionally, introduce a color-coded checklist process for food preparation, which delegates immediate responsibility and provides an easily trackable record. Have dedicated staff members whose role is strictly to oversee the safety components, such as ensuring proper labeling and handling of allergen-free dishes. Ensure these individuals are visibly present at the preparation stations, their presence serving as a physical reminder to the catering staff and providing immediate accountability.\n\nBy taking these steps, you create an environment where dietary restrictions are seen not as an additional task, but as a core component of service excellence that cannot be compromised. This proactive approach adds structure, clarity, and dedication to effective execution on the day",
